# Secrets and local state — never commit.
# Every .env variant, not just the bare one: .env.test and the .bak copies
# taken off the servers hold real tokens and real FERNET_KEYs, and a
# `git add -A` will happily stage them (it did, 2026-09-16, caught before
# the push). The example file is the one deliberate exception.
.env*
!.env.example
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Session logs — kept locally, decisions live in SPEC.md
history.md

# Runtime artefacts
logs/
*.pid

# Database copies, dumps, and the one-off scripts that make them (2026-09-14
# incident): they belong in backups/ and nowhere else, and none of it is ever
# committed. The three defensive patterns below are for the day somebody
# writes a dump into the repository root instead.
backups/
*backup*.json
*dump*.json
*tokens*.json
